WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.560
Ow, ow...

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.720
I can't move a damn muscle.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.940
What are we going to do with you?

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.240
I'll cast a healing spell now.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.110
I'm hungry.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.210
Lurie! Alma!

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.640
I thought Giluas beat that demon!

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.930
I thought he did, too.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.240
But its magical signature 
is vastly more powerful

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.880
than it was 
when they were fighting.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.970
<i>Impressive as ever, 
Matthias Hildesheimer.</i>

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.480
<i>I have a message for you.</i>

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:43.210
<i>I will soon destroy the seal 
and revive completely!</i>

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:47.400
<i>You may look forward to the day!</i>

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.440
Matty, what was that all about?

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.850
Someone was using powerful magic 
to animate the corpse.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.740
But the body couldn't take it.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.280
<i>The only one capable of such a feat...</i>

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.140
The big boss controlling the demon 
in the Melkia Dungeon.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.690
Was he behind these demidemons, too?

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.210
Hey...

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.750
Help a guy out, Matthias?

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.840
I think I'm gonna bleed out like this.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.050
Here, I'll help.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.470
Just hold still.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.820
That should restore your mobility.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.470
Don't push yourself like that again.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.110
Thanks, man. Appreciate it.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:25.300
All the commotion 
has really brought a crowd.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.140
The defeat of the demidemons must 
have lifted the Thought Paralysis.

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.520
Don't worry. I got this.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.150
I'll work things out for this city.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:39.840
I'm the Rank S adventurer, Giluas!

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.350
Under the Radinia Alliance's 
Emergency Authorization Act,

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.750
I hereby take control of Folkia!

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:50.310
Hang on. 
What is this "Emergency Authorization Act"?

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.410
If the person in charge 
of a given region goes missing,

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:58.130
a high-ranked adventurer 
can temporarily take control.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:01:59.890
Is this really the best idea?

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.840
Hey! Anyone here 
in a position of authority?

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.220
The guild branch head? 
The factory foreman?

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.160
I'm the foreman.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.690
Okay, awesome!

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:13.520
I officially appoint you 
provisional lord of Folkia!

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.600
He totally pawned it off.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.000
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.000
<b>The Strongest Sage Faces a Powerful Enemy.</b>

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.460
Here's your guild-issued permit.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:02.390
It'll let you enter 
Folkia's restricted area.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.680
Thanks. I'll head right out.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.560
Looks like I'll have to go back 
to square one in my training.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.550
Can't go around almost dying 
every time I slay one measly demon.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.150
See you someday.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:16.970
Right.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:22.440
<i>I can't wait to see how much he's grown 
the next time we meet.</i>

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:43.410
Here we are.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.470
This is the device we're after.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.760
Wow!

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.540
From an ancient magic super-civilization!

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.260
I wonder what technologies 
they used to make it!

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:55.100
These ruins seem to be 
from several thousand years ago.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:05:00.090
<i>I created them myself 
in my past life, in fact.</i>

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.450
Is this the device we're after?

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.860
Actually, the device is inside.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:09.870
Inside? But I don't see any sign 
of an entrance.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.960
You want me to bust us in?

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:15.030
My power's basically back to normal.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:18.440
I doubt even you could break 
through this, Iris.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.710
I made it out of 
extremely sturdy materials.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:22.160
You made it?

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:27.860
Well, maybe if Iris hit with everything she's got, 
she might put a dent in it.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.000
I get it!

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.610
The device is underneath!

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.350
Like when the ground opens up 
to reveal a staircase!

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:36.310
Not quite. 
The correct answer is here!

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.240
If you infuse it 
with magical power like this...

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.450
Great. It's still working.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.320
You figured that out 
on your first-ever visit!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.960
You're so smart, Matty!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.960
A-Anyway, let's head in!

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:59.230
I don't see anything to walk on, though.

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.170
That's intentional.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.090
We'll have to jump on down!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.180
Matty?!

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.970
Come on in! 
It's not that far down!

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.870
We should use...

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.160
...an Enhance Physique spell, right?

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.570
Come on, Iris. 
Take it easy.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.150
Sorry...

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:30.730
Hey, I see something!

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.730
Is this the device?

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:33.630
Yeah.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.990
I'll prepare the device for activation.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:40.710
In the meantime, go look around 
for anything we can use.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.950
"Anything we can use"?

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.800
It's an ancient ruin, after all.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:49.480
There might be old weapons 
or treasure scattered around.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:52.000
Treasure and weapons from ancient ruins!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.000
What an exciting thought!

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.830
We might really find something incredible!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:59.760
All right! 
Let's dig up some good weapons!

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:01.150
I'm counting on you both!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:04.040
There might be food, too!

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.640
I'm gonna get searching!

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:10.740
Even if there is food here, 
it'll be from thousands of years ago.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.000
Matty!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.480
I found something incredible!

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:21.690
"Something incredible"?

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:23.830
Yes! This sword!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.540
Th-That's...

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.650
<i>That sword I created 
on an all-nighter high,</i>

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.550
<i>designed to look cool 
and absolutely nothing else!</i>

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.050
<i>Did I forget to get rid of it 
before I reincarnated?</i>

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:37.820
<i>What was I thinking?</i>

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.330
Matty?

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.730
I found something, too!

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:46.480
<i>Not another cringey one 
I made in my past life, I hope...</i>

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:50.090
This spear is way too heavy 
for me to carry, but...

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.110
Iris might like it!

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.900
Iris has enough magical power 
to wield it,

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:58.660
but it's difficult to control 
and could be dangerous if she messes up.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.740
How would it be dangerous?

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:05.000
It would rapidly overheat, 
evaporating the user and everything around them.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.130
What?! 
That's way too dangerous!

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.140
If you don't channel magic into it, 
it's just a heavy spear.

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:15.640
Matthias! 
I found something really good!

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.640
<i>And here comes Iris...</i>

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:19.720
Look! Preserved foods from the ancients!

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:22.300
"Preserved foods"?

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:25.120
They do have a preserving spell 
cast on them,

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.690
but I'm not sure how well 
it would hold over millennia.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.090
We should be ready to go.

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:40.910
What is that?

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:43.790
A part from the refinery in Folkia.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:47.970
Analyzing it should let us 
track down the person

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.880
who gave the refining tech 
to the demidemons.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.260
A-Are you sure it's working right?!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.700
This wide-range magical-detection 
device can pick up

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:00.090
even the smallest magical signatures 
found in a piece of metal.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:04.030
I can extract the magical signature 
of anyone who's ever touched it.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.860
It stopped!

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.400
Seems like it worked.

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.450
This is the data from the magical analysis.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.820
There's definitely a demonic signature here.

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:21.220
I guess this is all 
I'll learn from this part.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.120
But, just as I thought...

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:26.290
It seems to be the same one 
that was giving orders

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.710
to the demon in the Dungeon City.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:31.800
You're saying that it was the same demon 
sending demons into Melkia

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:37.470
and controlling the demidemons in Folkia?

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:43.810
Yeah. And he might be working on a plan 
to destroy all of humanity.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.370
Destroy all of humanity?!

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:50.290
I acquired the demon's magical signature 
in the dungeon.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:51.760
I remember that!

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:52.860
Yes.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:58.320
Now we're going to use this 
to ascertain the demon's location.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.570
Here we go!

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.440
Wide Range Detect!

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:23.390
What's going on?

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.770
The seal is on the verge 
of being lifted.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.790
But it's not lifted yet, right?

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:33.460
And you're strong enough 
to put it back, right?

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:35.730
Matty?

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.660
He's a significantly dangerous opponent.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.950
His name is Zardias.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.340
We can't defeat him 
in our current state.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:51.590
You can't beat him either, Matty?

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.710
But there must be 
something we can do, right?

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:58.670
Basic tricks won't work on Zardias.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:01.540
Then the reason he was sealed...

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:04.980
Likely because the people of the time 
couldn't finish him off.

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:10.840
If we used immortality spells 
to train for hundreds of years,

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:13.000
we might eventually just manage 
to beat him.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:18.520
And if we went with that plan, 
we'd finish our training, beat him,

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:21.430
and then have to get 
to work rebuilding society.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:26.990
In the meantime, humanity would likely
be driven to near extinction.

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:31.580
You're saying that... 
even if we defeated the demon,

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:34.080
pretty much everyone except us would...

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:40.830
<i>I don't want to resort to that, either.</i>

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:43.700
<i>But I can't think 
of any other way to fight him.</i>

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:49.620
If only there were 
a really powerful weapon in these ruins.

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:53.640
But these all seem pretty useless.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:54.740
That's it!

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:55.520
Huh?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.130
Iris! Let me borrow that!

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.570
Matty?

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:03.510
I'm going to look for items with magical
signatures matching those in the ruins.

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:08.020
We'll use powerful magic items 
from elsewhere in the world against him.

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:12.640
<i>Because the weapons I made in my past life 
have ended up scattered all over the world.</i>

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:15.210
<i>If I could at least find that magic sword...</i>

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.340
There it is! And it's in...

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.510
...The capital of the Kingdom of Eis?!

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.970
<i>Did someone bring it in 
while we were gone?</i>

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:29.470
<i>With that magic sword...</i>

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:44.570
I'll give you these magistones 
while I have the chance.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:47.860
I designed them to react 
to the magic sword in question.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:51.530
If that magic sword really is 
in the royal treasury...

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:55.460
You'll have to bust in 
and justify your actions later.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.630
B-Bust in?!

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:05.380
That magical signature... was that...

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:06.720
Most likely Zardias.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.730
It appears he's completely broken the seal.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:12.760
Then the magical signature 
approaching us now...

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:15.510
Most likely Zardias coming after us.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:17.520
Huh? But that's bad!

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:19.410
He probably thinks 
that we're the one thing

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:22.360
standing in the way of his attack 
on humanity as a whole.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:28.450
Will Zardias attack us first, 
or will we find the magic sword first?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:31.910
It'll be a race against time.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:33.620
We're almost to the capital!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:34.700
Great.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.500
I'll hold off Zardias 
and buy us time.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:40.090
You two will have to find 
the magic sword without me.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.550
Understood!

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:46.260
<i>The great barrier over the capital 
should help prevent the demons from coming in.</i>

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.470
<i>But it won't work on Zardias.</i>

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:50.640
Matty.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:57.060
We will find that magic sword 
and bring it to you.

00:13:57.610 --> 00:14:00.510
So please, defeat Zardias!

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:02.770
We know that you can win!

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:05.150
We believe in you!

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.540
Right. Leave it to me.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:14.830
Did you feel 
a powerful magic signature just now?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:18.160
Yeah, that was really something.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.400
You think it's Matthias 
on the way back?

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:23.750
Huh? 
Doesn't it look like something's falling?

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:29.220
It's definitely pointing 
to the castle's treasury!

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:32.260
Let's take the shortest route there!

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.850
We'll keep falling on this course, 
then go straight to the castle!

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.460
Got it!

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:38.350
Wait! Hang on!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.850
How are we going to get 
through the barrier?!

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.970
That's right!

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:46.190
We don't have a spell 
to break through the barrier!

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:54.440
Huh? We're okay?

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:58.080
It seems as if the magistones 
had an enchantment for that!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.360
That's our Matty!

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:01.580
Indeed.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.310
Let's get going.

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:08.020
Was that Lurie and Alma?

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.130
Yeah.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.750
It should be about time.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:17.220
May I ask what you're doing, Matthias?

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:20.650
We've arrived at the capital 
ahead of Zardias.

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:23.440
I can't just sit around waiting 
for him to arrive.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.200
I have to prepare 
a first strike against him.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:30.690
He's currently traveling through a space 
available only to demons.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.990
It's the same transportation spell 
they used to attack the capital.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:39.710
I'm going to use the time before he arrives 
to seal the space itself.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:41.360
You can do that?

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:44.170
But if anyone could, 
it would be you.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.900
I have to take the chance.

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:48.920
Even if I fail, 
it should do some damage.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.330
It should buy us some time as well.

00:15:56.770 --> 00:15:58.550
I-It's a dragon!

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:01.180
Do you think the barrier will hold?!

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:02.880
Lots of people out.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.350
Wanna take a different route?

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.930
No, let's keep going straight.

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:09.820
Matty said he would buy us time!

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:13.650
The enemy we're fighting now isn't like
the ones he's taken out in one hit before.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:17.530
We have to get him that magic sword 
to turn the tables as quickly as we can.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:21.150
Matty said we should just bust in,

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:24.740
but wouldn't it be better to explain 
to the headmaster or His Majesty?

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:27.250
The fate of all humanity is on the line.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.920
I'm sure they would let us 
make a somewhat absurd request!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:34.930
Besides, we could easily break 
through the king's guard if we need to!

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.640
Listen to you, Lurie!

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:40.620
You're starting to think 
a little bit like Matty!

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.710
W-Well...

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:45.730
Lurie! Ahead of us!

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:49.450
That was close!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:52.360
Since we're already here, 
let's run along the rooftops—

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.370
Now!

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.530
This might just work!

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:08.130
No, it won't!

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:10.620
You failed?

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:13.840
Yeah. I'll just have to fight him.

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.210
Iris, can you use Dragon's Breath?

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.250
I can manage one blast, for sure!

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:33.080
I'm a little less sure 
about any more than that!

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.610
That should be enough.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.780
Fire off one, then pull back.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:41.010
Knowing that you're hiding nearby 
should help keep him in check.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:43.830
You don't need me to fight?

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:46.160
It's a lot for you to handle right now, Iris.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:48.980
So all I need from you 
is one big blast!

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.380
Understood!

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:53.380
Now!

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.420
One big...!

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:05.030
Did you see that?!

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:07.740
It's not just a dragon! 
There's a demon there, too!

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:08.770
Don't panic!

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.580
We have the barrier! 
We should be safe!

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:11.690
But...

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.650
Was that Zardias?

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:16.150
I think so. 
We have to hurry!

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.990
Dragon's Breath, eh?

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:24.330
Did you really think that such a pathetic attack 
would put a scratch on me?

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:30.100
But it woke me up for good, at least...

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:31.630
I've been waiting to meet you.

00:18:31.930 --> 00:18:34.430
Matthias Hildesheimer.

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:37.340
We've been searching for you as well.

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.020
Zardias.

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:43.930
<i>I didn't expect the Dragon's Breath 
to be particularly effective,</i>

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:46.270
<i>but I didn't expect him 
to completely shrug it off, either.</i>

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:50.590
<i>He seems to have significant skill 
and combat experience.</i>

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.180
I didn't come here to talk.

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:59.750
Let us proceed to the prelude 
to humanity's destruction!

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.160
I won't let that happen!

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:05.910
<i>He's aiming at...</i>

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.500
Iris! Move!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.710
Right!

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.540
Multilayer Barrier Defense!

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:16.950
<i>So much power in a single strike!</i>

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.880
Is he...

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.140
How weak you are.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.840
<i>He's not just powerful.</i>

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:28.100
<i>He's orders of magnitude faster 
than any other demon I've faced!</i>

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.100
<i>But...</i>

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.560
We're here!

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.060
State your names!

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:40.200
Lurie Abendroth and Alma Lepucius 
of Second Academy!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:44.160
We need a weapon from the treasury 
to deal with an emergency!

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.910
Please! Open the door!

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.160
I haven't heard about this!

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:52.100
I can't let anyone through 
without permission from His Majesty!

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:54.170
We'll get permission later!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:57.190
That's ridiculous! 
Surround them!

00:19:58.450 --> 00:19:59.850
I guess we don't have a choice.

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:02.470
Yes. We'll have to bust through!

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:03.720
Bandits, just as I thought!

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:07.070
Drop your swords, 
or we <i>will</i> arrest you!

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:08.660
Both sides, stand down!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.840
Your Majesty!

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:13.440
Lurie Abendroth.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:17.400
It appears that 
we're in a serious situation, yes?

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.430
Yes.

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:20.360
Matty is currently flying over the kingdom,

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:25.010
fighting a powerful demon 
for the fate of humanity!

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:29.240
He needs a weapon 
from the treasury to beat it!

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.040
Please, Your Majesty!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.020
Your Majesty!

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:33.990
Don't listen to these ruffians!

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:35.460
Open the door at once!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:36.920
This instant!

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:38.680
Yes, sir!

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:44.520
Now, hurry.

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:45.930
I'm sure there's no time to waste.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:48.510
Take what you need, quickly!

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:50.300
Thank you, Your Majesty!

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:56.270
They're moving so fast, 
I can't make it out!

00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:02.530
A pity. I'd assumed you had more 
to offer than this.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:09.450
<i>It's okay. 
I can still see his attacks coming.</i>

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:13.910
Oh? You didn't block that one?

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:15.220
Matthias!

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:17.130
<i>I thought I'd dodged them all,</i>

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:19.290
<i>but even the pressure 
of his swings is powerful...</i>

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.790
<i>He's truly something.</i>

00:21:22.480 --> 00:21:25.380
<i>If I fail to dodge once, 
I'm dead.</i>

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:29.470
<i>But blocking his attacks 
drains my magic power quickly.</i>

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:34.210
<i>It seems it's still going to take more time 
for Lurie and Alma to bring back the sword.</i>

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:37.180
<i>My chance of victory 
seems exceptionally low.</i>

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:41.690
You disappoint me, 
Matthias Hildesheimer.

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:45.170
Is this all the strongest 
in the world has to offer?

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.780
I suppose I should finish the job!

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:50.560
<i>Then, in order to win this battle,</i>

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:54.030
<i>I'll have to give up my life!</i>

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:28.290
If Matty's Crest of Failure 
is his strongest trait,

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:29.840
then maybe my energy is my strongest trait!

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:31.720
I'll bet mine is my appetite!

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:32.800
What about you, Lurie?

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:34.800
Me?

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:37.650
Maybe... my feelings for Matty...

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Episode 12 
The Strongest Sage Goes on a Journey Again.</b>

00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:39.630
"Feelings"...?
